flowchart TB
%% Figure 3: one week, from the week's end to the manager's decision. The dates
%% are the demand week's, w/e 13 Jun 2021, as the notebook prints them; the
%% reply deadline is the assumed 48 hours at level 2, from 10:00 on release day.
%% The steps sit on two rows, so that the smallest text prints at 8 pt or more
%% at a 16 cm column; each row's frame is drawn white, and the arrow between
%% the rows carries the forecasts on to the flag.
  subgraph ROW1[" "]
    direction LR
    W["<b>Week ends</b><br/>Sun 13 Jun 2021,<br/>the origin"]
    R["<b>PHS release</b><br/>Tue 22 Jun 2021"]
    F["<b>Forecast release<br/>horizons 1 to 4</b><br/>w/e 27 Jun to<br/>18 Jul 2021"]
    W -->|"9 days"| R --> F
  end
  subgraph ROW2[" "]
    direction LR
    L["<b>Flag, drift check,<br/>screen</b><br/>code sets the level"]
    B["<b>Demand brief</b><br/>Investigator drafts,<br/>Reviewer checks"]
    A["<b>Duty manager</b><br/>approves, edits or<br/>rejects; actions reply<br/>by Thu 24 Jun 2021"]
    L --> B --> A
  end
  ROW1 --> ROW2
  classDef code fill:#ffffff,stroke:#0b0b0b,stroke-width:2px
  classDef agents fill:#fde68a,stroke:#b45309,stroke-width:2px
  classDef person fill:#fecaca,stroke:#b91c1c,stroke-width:3px
  class W,R,F,L code
  class B agents
  class A person
